;; `de.explorama.backend.expdb.persistence.db-api` calls `(get (instances) ...)`,
;; but `instances` is inferred as a seq rather than the map its callers treat it
;; as. The contract is wrong, not the call sites, so the mismatch is reported at
;; every use and is not actionable from those sites. Whether it is reported at
;; all depends on which namespaces are already in clj-kondo's cache when the
;; file is linted, so it surfaces inconsistently between lint invocations.
{:lint-as {reagent.core/with-let clojure.core/let}
 :config-in-ns {de.explorama.backend.expdb.persistence.db-api
                {:linters {:type-mismatch {:level :off}}}}}
